                "name": "Kevin Tung",
                "email": "Kevin.Tung@quantatw.com",
                "username": ""
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/harma_mb_vr_infineon.json",
                    "line": 1277,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "@paligill@gmail.com Are we expecting the same VR firmware goes on all 3 devices?  That's a little surprising.  If it isn't the same exact image, we need to use different CompatibleHardware identifiers.\n\nGenerally the identifiers should be something like System.Model.Purpose.\n\nI don't know if we're thinking the \"Name\" is the differentiator here, but we should instead make sure the CompatibleHardware is entirely unique."
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/harma_mb_vr_infineon.json",
                    "line": 1277,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "> @paligill@gmail.com Are we expecting the same VR firmware goes on all 3 devices?  That's a little surprising.  If it isn't the same exact image, we need to use different CompatibleHardware identifiers.\n> \n> Generally the identifiers should be something like System.Model.Purpose.\n> \n> I don't know if we're thinking the \"Name\" is the differentiator here, but we should instead make sure the CompatibleHardware is entirely unique.\n\n@patrick@stwcx.xyz \nYes, the CompatibleHardware needs to be different if a different firmware image needs to go into the VR https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/phosphor-dbus-interfaces/+/80606/comment/c134b73b_a4919c20/.\n\nHaving said that there are 2 CompatibleHardware labels in this patch -\n\n1. com.meta.Hardware.Harma.VR.XDPE192C3B\n  -> Used by Harma_MB_vr_cpu0_vcore0, Harma_MB_vr_cpu0_vcore1\n2. com.meta.Hardware.Harma.VR.XDPE19283B\n  -. Used by Harma_MB_vr_cpu0_pvdd11\n  \n \nNow for #1 if the same firmware image will get deployed for both Harma_MB_vr_cpu0_vcore* then the CompatibleHardware is correct (which seems so based on name field), otherwise not. Would let @Kevin.Tung@quantatw.com confirm this?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/harma_mb_vr_infineon.json",
                    "line": 1277,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "11110128-KevinTung",
                        "email": "kevin.wtmh@gmail.com",
                        "username": "kevintungquanta"
                    },
                    "message": "For #1, the same firmware image will not be deployed to both Harma_MB_vr_cpu0_vcore*. Therefore, we need to use different CompatibleHardware identifiers. Do you have any suggestions for the identifier format?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/harma_mb_vr_infineon.json",
                    "line": 1277,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "How about following?\n\ncom.meta.Hardware.Harma.VR.XDPE192C3B_vcore0\ncom.meta.Hardware.Harma.VR.XDPE192C3B_vcore1\n\ncom.meta.Hardware.Harma.VR.XDPE19283B_pvdd11\n\nPlease raise a patch for PDI as well for this change."
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/harma_mb_vr_infineon.json",
                    "line": 1277,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "11110128-KevinTung",
                        "email": "kevin.wtmh@gmail.com",
                        "username": "kevintungquanta"
                    },
                    "message": "Added device-specific suffixes in the PDI: https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/phosphor-dbus-interfaces/+/80854"
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/harma_mb_vr_infineon.json",
                    "line": 1280,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "Can you please capitalize vr to VR in all the names?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/harma_mb_vr_infineon.json",
                    "line": 1280,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "11110128-KevinTung",
                        "email": "kevin.wtmh@gmail.com",
                        "username": "kevintungquanta"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                }
            ],
